+### data/bedrock/block_item_states.json
+
+This file records defaults, auxiliary variants, and legacy serialization names for Bedrock 1.26.51.1, protocol 2193.
+A pinned BDS Script API 2.9.0 fixture obtains defaults for all 1,477 registered blocks.
+The query removes virtual legacy accessor fields before comparing registered state properties.
+Exactly 26 defaults differ from canonical palette slot zero.
+
+A separate inventory fixture compares 4,950 numeric-data cases across 75 command-available block item types.
+It corrects the previous all-zero glow-lichen table, including the legacy face-bit remapping.
+The remaining curated auxiliary entries and serialization names retain the target reference data.
+These server checks do not independently verify the Windows client's cold auxiliary cache or custom archetype constructors.
+
+### data/bedrock/block_property_values.json
+
+The property values come from the original property serializers in Bedrock 1.26.51.1, build 51061372, protocol 2193.
+The private executable reference runs the complete property initializer and serializes all 708 observed ordinals across 118 property names.
+`direction` has a declared count of four, but chalkboards register sixteen values.
+The bundled block palette supplies each block's legacy ID, property set, domain count, and canonical order.
+These inputs reconstruct sparse descriptor metadata without a second per-block ID or offset table.
